    "body": "fix on issue/1053-fidelity-remaining-kinds · PR #1081 (stacked on #1064) · pinned by coarse_probe_plasma (a_ball_between_the_slacks_is_a_gouge_only_on_the_coarse_model, a_stem_between_the_slacks_is_a_shank_hit_only_on_the_coarse_model, the_probe_op_judges_with_its_models_excess, a_kerf_between_the_tolerances_is_refused_only_on_the_coarse_model, probe_and_plasma_are_judged_while_a_tolerance_is_left_and_refused_by_name_past_it) and coarse_laws::every_kind_is_either_judged_or_refused_for_a_stated_reason_on_a_reduced_model · merges after #1064\n\nPartial (Refs): probe and plasma are now judged. The cone and engrave rides stay refused permanently under this rule, because no tolerance holds the ride to the model; the reason is recorded in fidelity_law's header and docs/decisions/1053-fidelity-probe-plasma.md. **Still open here: the cross drill.** Its part law and rapids_radial each take a one-line tightening, but the chain is also proved by zero-slack mesh readings: cross_stock::standoff/rapids_clear, cross_entry, and drill_reach's reach and holder faces. Each of those needs the measured standoff grown by the excess, which moves the kernel's stations.",
